{
  "platform": "host",
  "provider": "Tool",
  "method": "listTools",
  "data": {
    "tools": [
      {
        "name": "cordis_inspect_list",
        "description": "List every Cordis Inspect Provider currently known to the Host, including local Host Providers and the latest manifests synchronized from the Client. Each entry includes its platform, purpose, read-only methods, and input/output schemas. Call this Tool before writing or configuring a plugin, then select the provider and method for cordis_inspect_query from its result. Do not guess names or treat an Inspect method as a business Service that Plugin code can call.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {}
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "cordis_inspect_query",
        "description": "Run a read-only query declared by an Inspect Provider. platform, provider, and method must come from cordis_inspect_list, and input must satisfy that method's schema. Use this Tool before writing plugin code to read exact Service methods, Event modes, plugin Config schemas, Tool schemas, theme tokens, or live Slot trees and props. Host queries run locally. A Client query waits for the first valid page response within the configured timeout; otherwise it reports a Client failure or asks you to reconnect and retry. This Tool cannot invoke business Service methods or modify the runtime.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "platform": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Runtime platform that owns the Provider.",
              "enum": [
                "host",
                "client"
              ]
            },
            "provider": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Exact Provider ID returned by cordis_inspect_list."
            },
            "method": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Exact method name declared by the Provider manifest."
            },
            "input": {
              "description": "Optional query input; it must satisfy the method input schema."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "platform",
            "provider",
            "method"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "propose_action",
        "description": "Show the user one optional action card under this answer. Call only as the skill that names the action instructs.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "action": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Action name from the skill."
            },
            "title": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Card title."
            },
            "brief": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "What the action does, in the user's language."
            },
            "details": {
              "type": "object",
              "description": "Fields the skill lists for this action.",
              "additionalProperties": true
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "action",
            "title",
            "brief",
            "details"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "ontoship_board_open",
        "description": "Open the OntoShip chain board in this session. Call once at the start of an autonomous chain (skill `chain`), in the orchestrator session only; executor and planning sessions do not call it. No arguments: the tool records this session in the workspace marker and the board opens in the right sidebar, live-following the unit's tickets. The board is visualization, not a gate.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {},
          "additionalProperties": false
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "working_directory",
        "description": "Read the current working directory, or change it with cd. Relative paths use the current directory. Existing shells and running processes keep their own directories.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "cd": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Existing directory to enter. Omit to read the current directory."
            }
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "create_worktree",
        "description": "Create a new Git branch and worktree from a local commit, branch, or tag, then change this session's working directory to it. Uncommitted files stay in the source checkout. Existing names fail. Use working_directory with cd to leave; the checkout and branch remain.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "name": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "New branch name, also used as the checkout directory: a few lowercase words joined by hyphens that describe the task, such as fix-login-retry. Omit to generate a unique name."
            },
            "from": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Local commit, branch, or tag to start from. Defaults to HEAD; no fetch is performed."
            }
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "team_task_create",
        "description": "Create one unowned pending task on the shared Team task board.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "subject": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Concise task title."
            },
            "description": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Complete task details and acceptance criteria."
            },
            "blocked_by": {
              "type": "array",
              "description": "Task ids that must complete first.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "write_scopes": {
              "type": "array",
              "description": "Advisory workspace-relative file or directory prefixes this task expects to modify.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "subject",
            "description"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "team_task_list",
        "description": "List shared tasks, including readiness, owner, revision, blockers, and write-scope warnings.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "status": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Optional exact status filter.",
              "enum": [
                "pending",
                "in_progress",
                "completed"
              ]
            },
            "owner": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Optional owner agent name filter; cannot be combined with unowned."
            },
            "unowned": {
              "type": "boolean",
              "description": "Filter tasks by whether they have no owner; cannot be combined with owner."
            },
            "ready": {
              "type": "boolean",
              "description": "Optional readiness filter."
            },
            "cursor": {
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "Zero-based result offset. Defaults to 0."
            },
            "limit": {
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "Number of rows, 1 through 100. Defaults to 50."
            }
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "team_task_get",
        "description": "Read the complete latest value of one shared task before changing or executing it.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "task_id": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Shared task id."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "task_id"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "team_task_update",
        "description": "Compare-and-set a shared task action using the latest revision from team_task_get or team_task_list.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "task_id": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Shared task id."
            },
            "expected_revision": {
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "Current task revision used as the CAS precondition."
            },
            "action": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Task transition to apply.",
              "enum": [
                "claim",
                "release",
                "edit",
                "set_dependencies",
                "complete",
                "reopen",
                "reassign",
                "delete"
              ]
            },
            "subject": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Replacement title for edit."
            },
            "description": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Replacement details for edit."
            },
            "blocked_by": {
              "type": "array",
              "description": "Complete blocker list for set_dependencies.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "write_scopes": {
              "type": "array",
              "description": "Replacement advisory write scopes for edit.",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "owner": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Agent name of the root or any continuable descendant for root-only reassign; omit to unassign."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "task_id",
            "expected_revision",
            "action"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "skill",
        "description": "Load the full instructions for a skill. Call it before acting on a task that names or clearly matches a skill in the session skill catalog.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "name": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "The exact skill name from the available skills list."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "name"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "read",
        "description": "Read a UTF-8 text file and return line-numbered content.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "file_path": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Path to read, resolved by the filesystem backend."
            },
            "offset": {
              "type": "number",
              "description": "1-based first line to return. Defaults to 1."
            },
            "limit": {
              "type": "number",
              "description": "Maximum number of lines to return. Defaults to 2000."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "file_path"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "glob",
        "description": "Find files, not directories, whose paths match a glob pattern, including hidden and ignored files. Returns up to 100 paths in modification-time order; a larger result keeps the first paths and reports where the complete list was saved.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "pattern": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Glob pattern to match file paths against (e.g. \"**/*.ts\", \"src/**/*.test.js\"). A pattern with no \"/\" matches the basename at any depth, so \"*\" and \"*.ts\" both search the whole tree; include a separator to anchor the depth."
            },
            "path": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Directory to search in. Defaults to the session workspace; a relative path resolves against it."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "pattern"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "grep",
        "description": "Search file contents with a ripgrep regular expression. Returns matching lines with line numbers, grouped by file. Returns up to 250 matches; a larger result reports where the complete match list was saved.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "pattern": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Regular expression to search for (ripgrep syntax)."
            },
            "path": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "File or directory to search. Defaults to the session workspace; a relative path resolves against it."
            },
            "include": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "One glob filter for which files to search (e.g. \"*.ts\", \"*.{js,jsx}\"). Not a list; negation is not supported."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "pattern"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "session_read",
        "description": "Read a live DSH session through the Host read API (read-only): projections snapshot, wait for a turn, history records, or the session/child list. Methods: `projections` (sessionId), `wait` (sessionId, timeoutMs?, afterSeq?), `events` (sessionId or parentSessionId+name), `list` (parentSessionId? or name?). A child subagent is addressed by its parent session id plus a name/label match; ambiguous and unknown children are named errors. Write/lifecycle methods (create/prompt/cancel/delete) are not available: this tool cannot start, steer or stop sessions. Credentials stay inside the plugin and never appear in results or errors.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "method": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Read method to call.",
              "enum": [
                "list",
                "wait",
                "events",
                "projections"
              ]
            },
            "sessionId": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Session id for projections/wait/events (ordinary session or child id)."
            },
            "parentSessionId": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Parent session id when addressing a child by name, or to filter `list`."
            },
            "name": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Child name/label/title match for events or list; requires parentSessionId."
            },
            "afterSeq": {
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "Exclusive output cursor for wait; omission includes available records."
            },
            "timeoutMs": {
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "Wait timeout in milliseconds; omission uses the Host default."
            },
            "maxMessages": {
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "Positive record limit for wait/events compaction."
            },
            "limit": {
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "List row limit when no parent/name filter is given."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "method"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "read_image",
        "description": "Read a PNG/JPEG/WebP/GIF file and return the image itself. Large images are downscaled automatically; do not install image libraries or create thumbnails to inspect an image.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "file_path": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Path to the image file, resolved by the filesystem backend."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "file_path"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "ask_user_question",
        "description": "Ask the user a concise question when you need confirmation, a choice, or missing information before proceeding. An answer item with empty selected and no custom means the user skipped that question: continue without it, do not ask it again, and do not treat the skip as permission.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "questions": {
              "type": "array",
              "description": "Questions to ask the user before continuing.",
              "items": {
                "type": "object",
                "additionalProperties": true,
                "properties": {
                  "id": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Stable id for this question; echoed in the answer."
                  },
                  "question": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The specific question to ask the user."
                  },
                  "header": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Optional short heading for the question, such as \"Confirm\" or \"Choose Mode\"."
                  },
                  "options": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "description": "Optional choices to show the user. If you recommend one, put it first and append \"(Recommended)\" to that label.",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "object",
                      "additionalProperties": true,
                      "properties": {
                        "label": {
                          "type": "string",
                          "description": "Short user-facing option label."
                        },
                        "description": {
                          "type": "string",
                          "description": "One sentence explaining the tradeoff or impact."
                        }
                      },
                      "required": [
                        "label"
                      ]
                    }
                  },
                  "multi_select": {
                    "type": "boolean",
                    "description": "Whether the user may select more than one option. Defaults to false."
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "id",
                  "question"
                ]
              }
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "questions"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "list_agents",
        "description": "List your entire subagent tree: the root agent and all reachable continuable descendants, including yourself. Rows carry names, descriptions, and status. A descendant's name is its path from the root, such as reviewer/checker. You can message any other agent in the subagent tree. running means it is working; inactive means no turn is executing; it does not indicate task completion, success, or failure. corrupt, unsupported, or unavailable means this row's own descendants could not be read; the row itself is still a member you can message. While you remain active, you will be notified when a direct child finishes; there is no need to keep checking its status. Use send_message to continue the conversation.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {}
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "wait_agent",
        "description": "Wait for input at your next step, including agent messages, completion notifications, and user steering. Returns immediately if new input is pending. `timedOut: false` means new input is pending. Pending input is delivered to the model after code execution finishes.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "timeout_ms": {
              "type": "integer",
              "description": "Wait duration in milliseconds, from 10000 through 3600000. Defaults to 30000."
            }
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "send_message",
        "description": "Send a message to an agent. A working agent receives it at its next step; an idle agent starts a new turn with it. Returns delivery confirmation.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "agent": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "The name of another agent in your subagent tree, as shown by list_agents."
            },
            "message": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "The message to deliver to the agent."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "agent",
            "message"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "list_subagent_models",
        "description": "Inspect the routes available for explicit subagent model selection. No arguments: authorized providers. `provider`: that provider's authorized models. `provider` + `model`: that model and its reasoning efforts. Query when choosing an explicit child route or reasoning effort. Omit optional fields rather than sending empty strings.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "provider": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Registered LLM provider id."
            },
            "model": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Exact model id; requires provider."
            }
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "subagent",
        "description": "Delegate a self-contained task to a subagent (a separate agent that works in its own context) to offload focused, independent work — research, a scoped implementation, an analysis — so it does not consume this conversation's context. The subagent returns its result, not its intermediate steps. This tool starts an independently managed subagent and immediately returns its name. If you are still online when it finishes, the runtime automatically delivers its completion notice. The notice includes the final answer unless the child sent you a message just before finishing. Use `send_message` to steer it while running or continue its conversation after it finishes. Omit `provider`, `model`, and `reasoning_effort` to use child defaults, falling back to compatible parent values.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "cwd": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Initial child working directory. Relative paths use your current directory; omitted inherits it. Later directory changes in either agent are independent."
            },
            "description": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "A short (3-5 word) description of the delegated task, for display. Use the language of the user's current request."
            },
            "name": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Optional short name for the subagent, unique among the subagents you create: lower-case letters, digits, and hyphens, starting with a letter, at most 32 characters; lead is reserved for the root agent. Omitted names default to agent-1, agent-2, and so on."
            },
            "prompt": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "The complete, self-contained task for the subagent. It does not share this conversation's context, so include everything it needs."
            },
            "agent_preset": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Agent preset for this child. Omit to use executor.",
              "enum": [
                "executor",
                "1c-executor",
                "scout"
              ]
            },
            "provider": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Child LLM provider id; requires `model`."
            },
            "model": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Model id within that provider; requires `provider`."
            },
            "reasoning_effort": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Reasoning effort id; requires `provider` and `model`. Omit to use the selected model's default, even when it matches the parent or configured route."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "description",
            "prompt"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "schedule_create",
        "description": "Create a 

[...]

   },
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "title": "tc_tableArguments"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "mcp__1c-testpilot__tc_calendar",
        "description": "Actions on type=\"CalendarField\" only. For a regular date input field, use tc_field(action=\"input_text\").\nAlso available: tc_field(action=\"is_visible\"), tc_field(action=\"is_enabled\"), tc_field(action=\"get_context_menu\"), tc_app(action=\"get_parent\").\n* marks a required action parameter; the group schema treats action parameters as optional. Pass action=\"name\" and only that action's parameters.\nok=true means accepted; verify effects by reading state. target_check: present, unknown (uncheckable), off (disabled); present does not prove an effect. target_hidden=true means the target exists but is invisible; it describes the element, not its ancestors. Its absence says nothing; hidden targets may still act (e.g. activate). Invalid addresses are rejected only where the address can be checked; an unverified empty read may mean a missing target. failure_context describes state/editor/choices; its complete=false means incomplete diagnostics.\nActions:\n- calendar_next_month(ref*)\n    Move a calendar field to the next month. The command is accepted, but nothing readable about\n    the field changes, so this cannot be verified. To move the date use tc_calendar(action=\"goto_date\").\n- calendar_next_year(ref*)\n    Move a calendar field to the next year. The command is accepted, but nothing readable about\n    the field changes, so this cannot be verified. To move the date use tc_calendar(action=\"goto_date\").\n- calendar_previous_month(ref*)\n    Move a calendar field to the previous month. The command is accepted, but nothing readable about\n    the field changes, so this cannot be verified. To move the date use tc_calendar(action=\"goto_date\").\n- calendar_previous_year(ref*)\n    Move a calendar field to the previous year. The command is accepted, but nothing readable about\n    the field changes, so this cannot be verified. To move the date use tc_calendar(action=\"goto_date\").\n- goto_date(ref*, year*, month*, day*)\n    Go to a date (year, month, day) in a calendar field. Returns changed/value_before/value_after.\nref selects the client; otherwise set connection_id when several clients are connected. Use tc_session(action=\"list_connections\").\nSuccess may omit target/connection echoes and shorten window details.\nUse returned references unchanged in ref; re-find expired elements.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "action": {
              "enum": [
                "calendar_next_month",
                "calendar_next_year",
                "calendar_previous_month",
                "calendar_previous_year",
                "goto_date"
              ],
              "title": "Action",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "connection_id": {
              "default": null,
              "title": "Connection Id",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "ref": {
              "default": null,
              "title": "Ref",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "year": {
              "default": null,
              "title": "Year",
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "month": {
              "default": null,
              "title": "Month",
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "day": {
              "default": null,
              "title": "Day",
              "type": "integer"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "action"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "title": "tc_calendarArguments"
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "mcp__1c-testpilot__tc_keyboard",
        "description": "Send a keyboard chord to the local 1C client or browse standard shortcuts offline.\nAlso available: tc_field(action=\"is_visible\"), tc_field(action=\"is_enabled\"), tc_field(action=\"get_context_menu\"), tc_app(action=\"get_parent\").\n* marks a required action parameter; the group schema treats action parameters as optional. Pass action=\"name\" and only that action's parameters.\nActions:\n- list_shortcuts(search=null, category=null, limit=20, offset=0)\n    Browse standard 1C shortcuts offline (omit connection_id): search English/Russian descriptions or ref names;\n    category filters by a returned category. Page with limit=1..100 and next_offset.\n    Each alternatives entry is a keys array for send_keys. Context/focus matters; the catalogue\n    contains standard managed-application PC shortcuts; availability depends on the platform version and configuration.\n- send_keys(keys*, ref=null)\n    Send one chord to local 1C. Without ref, use the active window and focused control.\n    ref addresses a window, managed form, input field or table: activates its window and,\n    for fields/tables, verifies focus before sending. Table columns are not targets.\n    Activation can finish pending input and switch pages; previous focus is not restored.\n    keys: zero or more CTRL/SHIFT/ALT modifiers followed by one ref, e.g. [\"CTRL\",\"SHIFT\",\"BACKQUOTE\"]\n    toggles panels. Letters A..Z, digits, F1..F12, ENTER/ESC/TAB, arrows, HOME/END,\n    PAGEUP/PAGEDOWN, INSERT/DELETE/BACKSPACE and punctuation/keypad names from list_shortcuts.\n    Requires Windows, Linux/X11 or macOS and local desktop access; on a shared Windows/Linux desktop\n    1C must have focus. macOS needs Accessibility permission; CTRL sends Command, ALT sends Option; INSERT is unavailable.\n    Successful delivery does not prove command success: read the resulting state.\n    May edit data, open dialogs or close windows.\n    Not text input; use input_text for text. Chords need not appear in list_shortcuts.\nref selects the client; otherwise set connection_id when several clients are connected. Use tc_session(action=\"list_connections\").\nSuccess may omit target/connection echoes and shorten window details.\nUse returned references unchanged in ref; re-find expired elements.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "action": {
              "enum": [
                "list_shortcuts",
                "send_keys"
              ],
              "title": "Action",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "connection_id": {
              "default": null,
              "title": "Connection Id",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "search": {
              "default": null,
              "title": "Search",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "category": {
              "default": null,
              "title": "Category",
              "type": "string"
            },
            "limit": {
              "default": null,
              "title": "Limit",
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "offset": {
              "default": null,
              "title": "Offset",
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "keys": {
              "default": null,
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
